  "body": "Found by mkinney's QA runs (p02, p03, p04, p05, p08) and reproduced on a minimal part by a separate verification run on 2026-11-18, CamCraft main `83867fd7` (= v0.24.0 code). Minimal repro projects and posted programs are kept on mkinney's machines and can be attached.\n\nWhat happens: a whole-model 2D Contour (no picks, defaults, stepdown 5) on a stepped part (base Z0-10 60x60, boss Z10-25 30x30, D10 end mill, flute 22) cuts the boss outline in 5 mm steps, but when the outline grows to the base below, the first pass on the base outline is taken at full depth: about 20 mm axial in a full-width 10 mm slot (with a 10 mm stock margin), plunged at F300. `verify` is ok with no findings and the program posts.\n\nWhy P1: a cut that breaks the tool or stalls the spindle posts silently (the axial depth is far over the stepdown and close to the full flute).\n\nRepro: the stepped block above; Tormach 770MX; fit stock (sides 3); WCS at the stock top centre; Face to z25; `add_operation contour source <model>` with defaults; generate, verify, post; read the Z of each pass per outline.\n\nRelated: #2460 (whole-model contour across lower outlines, merged), #2487.\n\nDone means: each new outline below Top Z is cut from the level where its material starts, in steps no deeper than the stepdown (or the op is refused by name), pinned by a test that reads the axial depth of every pass on this part.\n",
